D119|db-first-boot|defined|Boot sequence: (1) read IGOR_INSTANCE_ID + IGOR_DB_URL from .env — only these two ever required; (2) connect to DB; (3) compare .env mtime against last_env_read timestamp in instance DB record; (4) if newer: re-read full .env, push changed vars into system config subtree in DB, update last_env_read; (5) all runtime config comes from DB. .env is a change-trigger not a config store. If DB unreachable: fail fast, no env-var fallback. Two companion abstractions: System abstraction = DB subtree of shared config (model names, API key refs, feature flags, OR routing); Swarm abstraction = DB subtree of live instance topology (who is running, IP/port, role, last heartbeat) — replaces machines.json. Supersedes D116. Per-machine overrides stay in .env only when genuinely instance-specific; currently none beyond the two bootstrap vars.

