D126|graph-cache-postgres-migration|implemented-poc|Full substrate migration: SQLite eliminated everywhere. Two Postgres channels: IGOR_HOME_DB_URL (global truth, all Igor instances) + IGOR_LOCAL_DB_URL (box-scoped, shared by all instances on same box). make_db_proxy() splits into make_home_proxy() + make_local_proxy(). HOME tables: memories, interpretive_edges, wg_cooccur (WG master), notebooks, ResourceManager ledger/policy. LOCAL tables: ring_memory, twm_observations, pending_replies, my_top_N cache tracking, per-box resource metrics. Redis hot-cache per box for large frequently-traversed graphs (GraphCache abstraction): top N=10K words × M=50 co-occur, ~250MB, pre-warmed on boot, env-configurable, Igor-tunable at runtime. Write path: dual-write Redis + home; if home unreachable → write local + enqueue pending-replies row (key/value/attempt_count/last_attempt/resolved); retry on next access; 3rd failure → Worry to TWM. Worry = new TWM signal class: internal uncertainty, arousal↑ valence↓, high attractor_weight, persists until resolved. Cache maintenance: daily global_cache_refresh() prunes to top-N; each box tracks my_top_N; composition change → global_cache_flush() all boxes. Remote Igor boot: connect to home → world unfolds → local self-creates as needed. Supersedes D121, refines D122.
